  "description": "#5387 — `add_page_alias` and `remove_page_alias` through Undo. An alias edit appends a `remove_page_alias` per alias that goes and then an `add_page_alias` per alias that comes; `undo_ops` over those refs reverses each into the other, newest first, so the page holds what it held before. A respelling (`Plans` → `plans`) is a remove and an add of the same folded alias, which is why the order matters: undone the other way round, the remove of `plans` would take `Plans` with it. The refused third op pins the collision refusal on a page that holds nothing yet. Both alias op types and their reverses land in the op-log digest.",
